.TH XD\-MESSAGE 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-message \- show a Windows-style message box
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-message
.OP \-\-quiet
.RB [ \-\-error | \-\-warning | \-\-info ]
.I title
.I text
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-message
shows a message box with an icon,
.I text
and an OK button, in a window titled
.IR title ,
and plays the sound the sound scheme gives that kind of message.
It returns when the box is closed.
.PP
It is an internal helper of XeonDesktop, used by
.BR xd\-shell (1)
for messages such as errors renaming files and the battery alarms, but
scripts may use it too.
The options must come in the order shown.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Play no sound.
.TP
.B \-\-error
The error icon and the Critical Stop sound.
.TP
.B \-\-warning
The warning icon and the Exclamation sound.
.TP
.B \-\-info
The information icon and the Asterisk sound (the default).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-shell (1),
.BR xd\-sound (1)
